{"name":"Jack-O-Lantern","hex":"#d37a51","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jack-o-lantern","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of jack-o'-lantern."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jack-o-lantern"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jack-o'-lantern","blocks":[{"text":"A jack-o'-lantern is a carved lantern, most commonly made from a pumpkin, or formerly a root vegetable such as a mangelwurzel, rutabaga or turnip. Jack-o'-lanterns are associated with the Halloween holiday. Its name comes from the phenomenon of strange lights flickering over peat bogs, called jack-o'-lanterns. It is suggested that the name also has ties to the Irish legend of Stingy Jack, a drunkard who, after deceiving people throughout his life and even Satan, is doomed to roam the Earth with only a hollowed turnip to light his way."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Balle-%C3%A0-leunettes_10.jpg/330px-Balle-%C3%A0-leunettes_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack-o'-lantern","wikidata":"Q221009"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/RIP_Pumpkin.JPG/500px-RIP_Pumpkin.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/RIP_Pumpkin.JPG/1280px-RIP_Pumpkin.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/RIP_Pumpkin.JPG/500px-RIP_Pumpkin.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A picture carved onto a jack-o'-lantern for Halloween","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARIP_Pumpkin.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Traditional_Irish_halloween_Jack-o%27-lantern.jpg/500px-Traditional_Irish_halloween_Jack-o%27-lantern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Traditional_Irish_halloween_Jack-o%27-lantern.jpg/500px-Traditional_Irish_halloween_Jack-o%27-lantern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A plaster cast of a traditional Irish jack-o'-lantern in the Museum of Country Life, Ireland.  Rutabaga or turnip were often used.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATraditional_Irish_halloween_Jack-o'-lantern.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Thanksgiving_Greetings%2C_jack-o-lantern_and_a_turkey_%28NBY_18516%29.jpg/500px-Thanksgiving_Greetings%2C_jack-o-lantern_and_a_turkey_%28NBY_18516%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Thanksgiving_Greetings%2C_jack-o-lantern_and_a_turkey_%28NBY_18516%29.jpg/500px-Thanksgiving_Greetings%2C_jack-o-lantern_and_a_turkey_%28NBY_18516%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"American Thanksgiving Day postcard sent in 1909 with images of a jack-o'-lantern and a turkey","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThanksgiving_Greetings%2C_jack-o-lantern_and_a_turkey_(NBY_18516).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Halloween_2008_Pumpkin_workshop_2.jpg/500px-Halloween_2008_Pumpkin_workshop_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Halloween_2008_Pumpkin_workshop_2.jpg/1280px-Halloween_2008_Pumpkin_workshop_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Halloween_2008_Pumpkin_workshop_2.jpg/500px-Halloween_2008_Pumpkin_workshop_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jack-o'-l